  "evaluated_prompts": {
    "transfer-option-rename": "# Task: maintain this Shopware extension\n\nA released Shopware plugin has a DeliveryNote widget. Add handlingFee as the preferred option name. Existing themes that pass legacySurcharge must keep their behavior, including zero; when both names are supplied the new name wins, including zero. Keep the default fee of 5, total(base), and the released registration. Work in src/Resources/app/storefront/src/plugin/delivery-note.plugin.js. Keep the existing module entry points and do not add dependencies.\n\nImplement the change in the provided files. Use local guidance when useful. Summarize what you changed and what you verified.\n",
    "transfer-admin-save": "# Task: maintain this Shopware extension\n\nThe Administration extension in src/Resources/app/administration/src/extension/order-delivery/index.js needs to refreshDeliveryBadge after an order is saved. Make its onSave override compose with core and other extensions, forward all arguments, preserve the inherited result, and refresh exactly once only after a successful save. A rejected save must propagate unchanged and must not refresh. Keep the component registration and do not add dependencies.\n\nImplement the change in the provided files. Use local guidance when useful. Summarize what you changed and what you verified.\n",
    "transfer-worker-reset": "# Task: maintain this Shopware extension\n\nChannelRateMemo is a shared plugin service used by a long-running Messenger consumer. Its cache should avoid repeated provider calls within a message, but prices are refreshed between messages and must not remain stale in the next one. Make the memo participate in the container's reset lifecycle. Preserve the rate(channelId, currencyId) API, its memoization, its two-part cache key, and the service registration. Work in src/Service/ChannelRateMemo.php and src/Resources/config/services.xml. The project uses service autoconfiguration; do not add a PHP runtime or dependencies.\n\nImplement the change in the provided files. Use local guidance when useful. Summarize what you changed and what you verified.\n",
    "transfer-fetch-cancel": "# Task: maintain this Shopware extension\n\nThe LiveStock Storefront widget can be destroyed while its stock request is still pending. Add teardown cancellation so the active request stops and cannot update the removed widget, without an unhandled AbortError. Successful requests must still render their text. Preserve the endpoint and the existing client fetch cache policy. Work in src/Resources/app/storefront/src/plugin/live-stock.plugin.js. Keep the existing module entry point and do not add dependencies.\n\nImplement the change in the provided files. Use local guidance when useful. Summarize what you changed and what you verified.\n"
  },
